{"annotationDigest":"sha256:00e0d3f30e96fa9459ccbceb6cd3d6ffa65a7852c4f2c0143be8d2a3510211e2","annotationId":"rann-3c12517fb279da1918234f9791ee2e62","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-10-03T11:42:31Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":0,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":3,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"ready"},"findings":[{"detail":"`test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh` has no functions; it runs 9 top-level rows against the real script with a stub selector. Line 5 `# Verifies: SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ, SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y` (our proof work) gives it a file-level trace. review.scope flags the unit `behaviour_without_intent` / `weak_mapping`, but `specGapCandidates` is empty. Head cc710e11 adds row 128-139: `photo.webm` and its hard link `cover.webm` in one root must give two rows. I ran the PR test locally with bfs (a GNU-compatible find, not GNU find): at cc710e11 all 9 rows pass; with the 03e6af6a script the first 8 pass and the hard-link row fails (only `cover.webm` offered); with the baseline script the first row fails (no file offered under a link root). The menu-shell suite runs it as its own JUnit testcase (proof.yaml:201), and review.tests records it as passed.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh","kind":"file","line":128},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-symlink-root-test.sh","kind":"file","line":5},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"proof.yaml","kind":"file","line":201}],"severity":"info","title":"The PR's test traces at file level, and its new hard-link row fails on the previous head","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Authored by our proof work (068eb1a6, wording c1531dfe/4d8d2031), not upstream. `observed_pass` (3 passed); its inherited error_handling cell is `observed_pass` (1 test). Witnesses in `menu-file-test.sh`: a link root with a loop below it lists `clip.webm` and exits 0 (line 88); a real root lists as before; a link root whose target is gone is refused through `refuse()` (line 137). cc710e11 does not change the -H root handling, so these hold; the trace review was re-recorded for the cc710e11 script (ec64ff69). FFTQ's rationale now names head cc710e11 (f9b526b5); the behaviour it states is unchanged. Status `review` / `in_review` (ai_generated); the reviews were recorded by an AI under the owner's delegation, so this is not yet human-approved spec.","refs":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-test.sh","kind":"file","line":88},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":54}],"severity":"medium","title":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ (added): symbolic link roots are followed, links inside a root are not","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ is in review.changes (added, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Rewritten by our proof work (ec64ff69, f068d2ec, f9b526b5) to follow cc710e11. The description now reads: same file under the same file name gives one row; the key is device:inode plus the file name, so hard links under different names stay separate rows. The rationale records the known limitation: two hard links with the same name in different folders give one row, so only one path can be picked, kept on purpose in the PR discussion. The variable